# npm launcher package

Ships the native binary of the rust-cli instance named like the `bin` key in `package.json`; it
needs a rust-cli instance named `{{ crate }}` in `crates/{{ crate }}`.

- `bin/launcher.js` resolves `<name>-<platform>-<arch>` with `createRequire`, runs it with inherited
  stdio, forwards the exit code and re-raises a signal. `<BIN>_BINARY` (bin name upper-cased,
  `-` to `_`) points it at a local build.
- Never add `postinstall`, `preinstall`, a download or network code; never commit
  `optionalDependencies` or `repository` (`scripts/stage.mjs` writes both at release time).
- `scripts/stage.mjs` turns release artifacts into `dist-npm/`; the platform list is `TARGETS`.
- `version` here and in `crates/{{ crate }}/Cargo.toml` must match; bump both together.
  `test/version-sync.test.js` checks it.
- `typecheck` is `node --check` (no `@types/node` in the catalog for `tsc`); `test` and `typecheck`
  do not build the crate.
- A human pushes the tag `{{ crate }}-v<version>`; the release workflow publishes the platform
  packages, then the launcher.
